From 6bba141d1f5abf0292a0dcb23a6d1d2b74874fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:35:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cat-engine): novel-block design + learning-rate readout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the learning-rate fix the psychometric sweep specified: a
30-trial single-domain block at adaptive difficulty (half the items of
four shallower blocks, and better recovery), fitted with the joint MAP
learning-curve estimator instead of the OLS score slope.

The readout returns an ordinal band and never a bare number, because the
MAP estimate is shrunk ~60% toward zero. It returns `indeterminate`
whenever the posterior is too wide to separate bands — which, measured
here, is the case at the recommended block length: one child's SE is
~0.039 against a population spread of ~0.030. Ranking a cohort (r~0.62)
and placing an individual are different claims and only the first holds,
so `learningRateCohortRank` is provided as the supportable alternative.

Named `learning-block` rather than `phase2` to keep the engine
structure-agnostic. The rate is deliberately kept out of the scored
decision payload; it remains a labelled hypothesis.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
